module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.InfinitesimalDeformationSelfMapHomSectionValue
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Geometric.SchemeDeformationSelfMapIdealScaling

/-!
# A self-arrow of a deformation on the perturbation of a lift

Let `P` be a first-order deformation of `X` over a base whose maximal ideal is square-zero and
generated by `t`, and let `φ : P ⟶ P` be a self-arrow whose base component scales `t` by `c`.
`Deformation.Examples.conormalSelfMap_eq_smul` computes the endomorphism `φ.map` induces on the
conormal sections of the special fibre: it is multiplication by the function the residue of `c`
determines on `X`.

This file feeds that computation to
`Stacks.Thickenings.homSectionValue_comm_of_conormalSelfMap_eq_smul`. The outcome is the
hypothesis `hθ` of
`Stacks.Thickenings.liftsOverBaseVAddOfBase_comp_of_homSectionValue_comm` — the naturality of
the action of [Stacks Project, Tag 0CK2] in the thickening — at a pair of self-arrows of one
situation. That naturality is what the scalar half of the `k`-linearity asserted in
[Stacks Project, Tag 0E3V] consumes: the scalar action on the tangent module is transport along
`Deformation.tangentScaling`, whose realisation on total spaces is a self-arrow of exactly this
kind.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.conormalSelfMap_eq_baseSection_smul_of_le`:
  `Deformation.Examples.conormalSelfMap_eq_smul` with its scalar presented as the restriction of
  one section over a fixed ambient open, which is the shape the bridge consumes.
* `Deformation.Examples.homSectionValue_comm_of_selfMap`: **the perturbation of a lift of `f` to
  a pair of first-order deformations commutes with a pair of self-arrows**, when the acting
  section is scaled by the function the residue of the base scalar determines.

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis on the second acting section is left as the pointwise statement `hθ` rather than
as `θ₂ = c • θ₁`: the sections of a sheaf of homomorphisms over a general open carry no scalar
action in the library — only the `k`-structure transported at `⊤` by
`Deformation.Examples.deformationHomSectionsTopModule` — so `c • θ₁` cannot be written at a
general `V`, and at `⊤` it is a transport with no formula on sections. The pointwise form is
what a consumer must produce in either case.

The self-arrow on the target side is only required to fix the special fibre of `Q`
(`ψ.special_compat`) and to be compatible with the lift (`cA`); nothing is assumed about its
base component. That asymmetry is genuine — the computation of the conormal endomorphism is
needed only on the source, since the perturbation takes its values in `𝒞_{X/P.scheme}`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CK2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CK2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DY7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E3V)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Deformation.Examples

variable {Λ k : Type u} [CommRing Λ] [Field k] [Algebra Λ k]
variable {X Y : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))}

attribute [local instance] deformationSpecialMap_isClosedImmersion

/-! ### The scalar as the restriction of one section -/

/-- **The endomorphism of the conormal sections induced by a self-arrow, with its scalar read as
the restriction of a section over a fixed ambient open.** This is
`Deformation.Examples.conormalSelfMap_eq_smul` with
`Deformation.Examples.baseSection_map` applied to its right-hand side, so that one section over
`P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ V` serves for every open `A ≤ V` at once. That is the form the hypothesis `hc`
of `Stacks.Thickenings.homSectionValue_comm_of_conormalSelfMap_eq_smul` asks for. -/
theorem conormalSelfMap_eq_baseSection_smul_of_le
    {P : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X}
    (hsq : P.specialMap.ker ^ 2 = ⊥) (φ : P ⟶ P) {t c : (P.base : Type u)}
    (ht : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (P.base : Type u) = Ideal.span {t})
    (hb : φ.base.hom t = c * t) (V : P.scheme.Opens) (A : P.scheme.Opens) (hA : A ≤ V)
    (x : Γ(Stacks.Thickenings.conormalModules P.specialMap, P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ A)) :
    Stacks.Thickenings.conormalSelfMap hsq φ.special_compat A x
      = (X.left.presheaf.map (homOfLE (P.specialMap.preimage_mono hA)).op).hom
          (baseSection X.hom (Deformation.Artin.residueMap P.base c)
            (P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ V)) • x := by
  rw [conormalSelfMap_eq_smul hsq φ ht hb A x,
    baseSection_map X.hom (Deformation.Artin.residueMap P.base c)
      (P.specialMap.preimage_mono hA)]

/-! ### The perturbation under a pair of self-arrows -/

/-- **The perturbation of a lift of `f` commutes with a pair of self-arrows of the two
deformations.** Let `P` and `Q` be first-order deformations of `X` and `Y`, let `b` be a lift of
`f` to them over an open `V` of `P.scheme`, let `φ : P ⟶ P` be a self-arrow whose base component
multiplies a generator `t` of the maximal ideal of `P.base` by `c`, let `ψ : Q ⟶ Q` be a
self-arrow, let `w` be a self-map of `V` lying over `φ.map`, and let the lift be compatible,
`b ≫ ψ.map = w ≫ b`. If the acting section `θ₂` is the function the residue of `c` determines
times `θ₁`, then the two perturbations `Stacks.Thickenings.homSectionValue` correspond under
`w^♯` and `ψ.map^♯`.

This is the hypothesis `hθ` of
`Stacks.Thickenings.liftsOverBaseVAddOfBase_comp_of_homSectionValue_comm` at a self-arrow of one
situation, which is the shape the scalar half of the `k`-linearity of
[Stacks Project, Tag 0E3V] needs: it says that acting by `c · θ` and pushing a lift forward
along the coordinate scaling are the same operation on perturbations.

It is **not** the `k`-homogeneity of
`Deformation.Examples.schemeMorphismDerivationTangentMap`: that needs in addition the
naturality theorem itself, an arrow of the deformation category of `f` built from the pair
`(φ, ψ)`, and the identification of the base component of that arrow with
`squareZeroExtensionArtinian.map (c • 𝟙 M)`. -/
theorem homSectionValue_comm_of_selfMap {S : Scheme.{u}}
    {P : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X}
    {Q : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) Y}
    (hsq : P.specialMap.ker ^ 2 = ⊥) (pQ : Q.scheme ⟶ S)
    (φ : P ⟶ P) (ψ : Q ⟶ Q) {t c : (P.base : Type u)}
    (ht : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (P.base : Type u) = Ideal.span {t})
    (hb : φ.base.hom t = c * t)
    {f : X.left ⟶ Y.left} {V : P.scheme.Opens} {b : V.toScheme ⟶ Q.scheme}
    (cb : P.specialMap ∣_ V ≫ b = ((P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ V).ι ≫ f) ≫ Q.specialMap)
    {w : V.toScheme ⟶ V.toScheme} (hw : w ≫ V.ι = V.ι ≫ φ.map)
    (cA : b ≫ ψ.map = w ≫ b)
    {θ₁ θ₂ : Stacks.Thickenings.deformationHomSections P.specialMap f
      (Q.specialMap ≫ pQ) V}
    (hθ : ∀ (U : X.left.Opens) (hU : U ≤ P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ V)
        (y : Γ(Stacks.Smooth.pullbackCotangentSheaf (Q.specialMap ≫ pQ) f, U)),
      θ₂.app hU y
        = (X.left.presheaf.map (homOfLE hU).op).hom
            (baseSection X.hom (Deformation.Artin.residueMap P.base c)
              (P.specialMap ⁻¹ᵁ V)) • θ₁.app hU y)
    (W : Q.scheme.Opens) (s : Γ(Q.scheme, W)) :
    (V.toScheme.presheaf.map (eqToHom (Stacks.Thickenings.preimage_comp_eq cA W)).op).hom
        ((w.app (b ⁻¹ᵁ W)).hom
          (Stacks.Thickenings.homSectionValue hsq pQ cb θ₁ W s))
      = Stacks.Thickenings.homSectionValue hsq pQ cb θ₂ (ψ.map ⁻¹ᵁ W)
          ((ψ.map.app W).hom s) :=
  Stacks.Thickenings.homSectionValue_comm_of_conormalSelfMap_eq_smul hsq pQ
    φ.special_compat cb hw ψ.special_compat cA
    (conormalSelfMap_eq_baseSection_smul_of_le hsq φ ht hb V) hθ W s

end Deformation.Examples

end
